WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.173
Allow 4 minutes.

00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:04.037
Course completion is an implementation measure.

00:00:04.277 --> 00:00:09.504
It does not establish that handoffs improved, or that any improvement was caused by the course.

00:00:09.744 --> 00:00:16.016
A useful plan separates learning evidence, workplace behavior, and conditions that enable the behavior.

00:00:16.706 --> 00:00:23.767
Worked example: before the fictional rollout, inspect a comparable sample of handoffs for all three required elements.

00:00:24.007 --> 00:00:26.653
During training, collect decision-check results.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:31.458
After rollout, inspect another comparable sample and record missing elements.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:39.271
Ask supervisors whether staff can access the owner list, have time to complete the form, and receive consistent expectations.

00:00:39.511 --> 00:00:44.162
A simultaneous form redesign could also explain changes in performance.

00:00:44.852 --> 00:00:47.156
Give the team a one-screen handoff checklist.

00:00:47.396 --> 00:00:54.671
Ask managers to review the first few attempts, correct errors privately, and route tool-access problems to the system owner.

00:00:54.911 --> 00:01:02.719
If staff can perform correctly in practice but lack production permissions, another explanation video will not grant those permissions.

00:01:03.409 --> 00:01:13.013
Transfer task, 60 seconds: write a plan containing one practice task, one support available at the point of work, one responsible person, and one

00:01:13.013 --> 00:01:15.014
observable behavior to review.

00:01:15.254 --> 00:01:23.510
Sample: “Agents route two practice cases; the team lead pins the rule card and reviews whether next week’s sampled handoffs name an owner.”

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.288
Now it's your turn.

00:01:25.528 --> 00:01:29.240
Agents pass practice but cannot open the owner list in production.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.549
What should the rollout lead prioritize?

00:01:31.789 --> 00:01:34.904
Pause the video and make your choice in the activity below.

